# Week 3 — Urdu OCR Dataset Preparation

Building a PyTorch Dataset class for the Urdu OCR model.

## Why This Matters

A machine learning model needs image-text pairs so that it can learn how visual Urdu text corresponds to the correct written text. A properly prepared dataset makes it easier to train and evaluate an OCR model.

## Live Demo

[Urdu OCR Hugging Face Space](PASTE_YOUR_HUGGINGFACE_SPACE_LINK_HERE)

## How It Works

The Urdu images and their corresponding text labels were loaded into a custom PyTorch Dataset class. Each image was processed using the TrOCR processor, while the corresponding Urdu text was converted into token IDs for the model. The dataset was then divided into training and testing sets so the model could later be trained and evaluated on separate data.

## What I Did

- Loaded the Urdu image dataset.
- Loaded the ground-truth labels.
- Created a custom `UrduOCRDataset` class.
- Loaded the TrOCR processor.
- Processed Urdu images into model-compatible inputs.
- Converted text labels into token IDs.
- Tested the dataset class.
- Created a train-test split.

## Results

- Urdu image-text dataset successfully loaded.
- Custom PyTorch Dataset class created.
- Images and text labels successfully connected.
- Dataset prepared for TrOCR model training.
- Train-test split created:
  - 80% Training
  - 20% Testing

## Model

The TrOCR processor used for the dataset preparation was:

`microsoft/trocr-base-printed`

